{"t": 182.735, "dir": "out", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/didOpen", "params": {"textDocument": {"uri": "file://~/workspace/rf-mcp-robotcode/experiments/robotcode-remote/round3/agent_lsp/probe/p_plain/resources/shop.resource", "languageId": "robotframework", "version": 1, "text": "*** Settings ***\nDocumentation     Page objects for the demo shop. Use ONLY these keywords in tests.\nLibrary           Browser\nLibrary           RequestsLibrary\n\n*** Variables ***\n${SHOP_URL}         http://127.0.0.1:8765/shop.html\n${API_URL}          http://127.0.0.1:8765\n${FINDER_INPUT}     css=input#product-finder\n${HIT_ROWS}         css=ul#hits > li\n\n*** Keywords ***\nLaunch Storefront\n    [Documentation]    Opens a fresh headless browser on the shop start page.\n    [Arguments]    ${headless}=True\n    New Browser    chromium    headless=${headless}\n    New Page    ${SHOP_URL}\n\nType Into Product Finder\n    [Documentation]    Types ``term`` into the product finder box and submits it with Enter.\n    [Arguments]    ${term}\n    Fill Text    ${FINDER_INPUT}    ${term}\n    Keyboard Key    press    Enter\n\nHit Count Should Be\n    [Documentation]    Asserts that exactly ``expected`` result rows are shown.\n    [Arguments]    ${expected}\n    Get Element Count    ${HIT_ROWS}    ==    ${expected}\n\nProbe Catalog Endpoint\n    [Documentation]    GETs ``path`` from the catalog API and returns the response.\n    [Arguments]    ${path}    ${expected_status}=200\n    Create Session    catalog    ${API_URL}\n    ${resp}=    GET On Session    catalog    ${path}    expected_status=${expected_status}\n    RETURN    ${resp}\n"}}}}
{"t": 182.736, "dir": "out", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "method": "textDocument/hover", "params": {"textDocument": {"uri": "file://~/workspace/rf-mcp-robotcode/experiments/robotcode-remote/round3/agent_lsp/probe/p_plain/resources/shop.resource"}, "position": {"line": 21, "character": 6}}}}
{"t": 182.742, "dir": "in", "msg": {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"contents": {"kind": "markdown", "value": "### Keyword *Fill Text*\n\n#### Arguments: \n\n| | | | |\n|:--|:--|:--|:--|\n| `selector`| : `str` |  |  |\n| `txt`| : `str` |  |  |\n| `force`| : `bool` | = | `${False}` |\n\n**Tags**: \n- PageContent\n- Setter\n\n#### Documentation:\nClears and fills the given `txt` into the text field found by `selector`.\n\n\nThis keyword waits for an element matching the `selector` to appear, waits for actionability checks, focuses the element, fills it and triggers an input event after filling.\n\n\nIf the element matching the selector is not an \\<input>, \\<textarea> or [contenteditable] element, this keyword fails. Note that you can pass an empty string as `txt` to clear the input field.\n\n\n| Arguments | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `selector` | Selector of the text field. See the `Finding elements` section for details about the selectors. |\n| `txt` | Text for the text field. |\n| `force` | Set to `True` to skip Playwright's [Actionability checks](https://playwright.dev/docs/actionability). |\n\n\nKeyword uses strict mode, see `Finding elements` for more details about strict mode.\n\n\nSee `Type Text` for emulating typing text character by character.\n\n\nExample:\n\n\n```text\n`Fill Text`    css=input#username_field    username\n```\n\n[Comment >>](https://forum.robotframework.org/t//4254)\n\n"}, "range": {"start": {"line": 21, "character": 4}, "end": {"line": 21, "character": 13}}}}}
